   "answer": "For an executable hook, the analogue of a code mutant is a published syntactic operator on hook source plus an independent behavioural oracle. On the real Stop-hook command-center/p2-wave/probes/ARC-0005/stop_hook.py, operators were hashed (0faef7859e78…) before rates. 5/7 mutants were killed; survival rate=0.2857. Control H-LVR-NEVER-FIRE was killed (never-fire still silent on drifted trees). Survival means something here only because (1) the operator set was frozen first, (2) the oracle is independent of the mutant, (3) a known-breaking control was killed, proving the suite is not silent. H-AOR-SWAP-ARGS survived because detect() is symmetric in its two trees; H-NOOP-COMMENT is equivalent by construction. For skills and rules the same operators can be written as text transforms (MUST→MAY, drop a constraint, negate a MUST-NOT) but a survival rate is NOT-ESTABLISHED: this worktree has no mechanical oracle for those artifacts, and a rate without an oracle measures nothing. SUCCESS:RES-0090 in the receipt AND a pre-published operator set plus a measured survival rate on one real hook with a killed control",
